<p>What follows is reproduced in John's own words, exactly as he wrote them — nothing edited, softened, or left out. It carries the same broad, joking, tall-tale narrator he uses throughout "Please Go to Hell" and "Once Around the Thunder Mug," playing up a folksy small-town-goofball persona that was a deliberate comic choice, not a reflection of how he actually wrote or spoke. Where a spelling or spacing slip appears below, it is almost certainly an artifact of scanning and optical character recognition on the original printed book, not an error of John's.</p>

<p>John signed his newspaper column and this and his other self-published books with the pen name "Thundermug."</p>

